WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Build with Accessibility — Android accessibility auditing on your device.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Screen access requires explicit consent. The disclosure explains what is read and how it is used.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Enable Build with Accessibility in Android Accessibility settings.

4
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Android displays its own access confirmation and shortcut instructions.

5
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
The floating capture button is optional. Other capture controls are also available.

6
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Open the synthetic fixture and tap the logo button to capture the current screen.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Review the evidence and approximate reading-order prediction. Actual TalkBack testing remains necessary.

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Captured conditions accompany findings. Missing accessible names are flagged with confidence and severity.

9
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
The finding detail highlights the affected control in the captured screen.

10
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Use the manual checklist to record tests that automation cannot complete.

11
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Sessions keep captures, review notes and outcomes together.

12
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.500
Keyboard focus is visibly outlined. Audits stay on the device until the user exports them.
